# Append to the .gitignore of the repository being documented.
#
# The durable artifacts are committed. A registry_hash match skips module
# analysis, which presumes the registry and the API snapshot are already on
# disk, and the grounding check reads api-surface.json on every run. Under CI
# caching a cold cache produces a matching hash with nothing behind it.
# Each run writes into `.docs-gen/<ticket>/`, so the durable artifacts are one
# level deeper than the root. The clones and the downloaded Vale packages sit
# in the root itself and are never committed.
.docs-gen/*
!.docs-gen/*/
.docs-gen/*/*
!.docs-gen/*/registry.json
!.docs-gen/*/api/
!.docs-gen/*/api-surface.json
.docs-gen/checkouts/
.docs-gen/vale-packages/
